    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U06-L19-ACTIVITY-003",
      "SourceSection": "19.2: Watching the Evening Sky",
      "SourceExcerpt": "The data from the warm-up is the amount of the Moon that is visible from a particular location on Earth at midnight for each day in January 2018. A value of 1 represents a full moon in which all of illuminated portion of the moon's face is…",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u06-l19.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U06-L19-ACTIVITY-004",
      "SourceSection": "19.2: Watching the Evening Sky",
      "SourceExcerpt": "What is an appropriate midline for modeling the Moon data? What about the amplitude? Explain your reasoning.",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u06-l19.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U06-L19-ACTIVITY-005",
      "SourceSection": "19.2: Watching the Evening Sky",
      "SourceExcerpt": "What is an appropriate period for modeling the Moon data? Explain your reasoning.",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u06-l19.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U06-L19-ACTIVITY-006",
      "SourceSection": "19.2: Watching the Evening Sky",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Choose a sine or cosine function to model the data. What is the horizontal translation for your choice of function?",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u06-l19.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U06-L19-ACTIVITY-007",
      "SourceSection": "19.2: Watching the Evening Sky",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Propose a function to model the Moon data. Explain the meaning of each parameter in your model and specify units for the input and output of your function.",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u06-l19.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U06-L19-ACTIVITY-008",
      "SourceSection": "19.2: Watching the Evening Sky",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Plot the data using graphing technology and check your choice of parameters (midline, amplitude, period, horizontal translation). What changes did you make to your model?",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u06-l19.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U06-L19-ACTIVITY-009",
      "SourceSection": "19.2: Watching the Evening Sky",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Use your model to predict when the next two full moons will be in 2018. Are your predictions accurate?",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u06-l19.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U06-L19-ACTIVITY-010",
      "SourceSection": "19.2: Watching the Evening Sky",
      "SourceExcerpt": "How much of the Moon do you expect to be visible on your birthday? Explain your reasoning.",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u06-l19.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U06-L19-ACTIVITY-011",
      "SourceSection": "19.2: Watching the Evening Sky",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Sometimes a phenomenon can be periodic even though it is not connected to motion in a circle. For example, here is a graph of the water level in Bridgeport, Connecticut, over a 50 hour period in 2018.",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u06-l19.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U06-L19-ACTIVITY-012",
      "SourceSection": "19.2: Watching the Evening Sky",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Notice that each day (or each 24 hour period) there are two tides, a small one where the water goes up to a little less than 3 feet and then a bigger one when the tide goes up to a little more than 3 feet. Since there are two tides per…",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u06-l19.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U06-L19-ACTIVITY-013",
      "SourceSection": "19.2: Watching the Evening Sky",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Putting together all of our information gives model \\(f(h) = 3\\sin\\left(\\frac{2\\pi}{12}(h -1)\\right)\\), where \\(h\\) measures hours since midnight on September 1.",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u06-l19.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U06-L19-ACTIVITY-014",
      "SourceSection": "19.2: Watching the Evening Sky",
      "SourceExcerpt": "The coefficient of 3 is the amplitude, which averages out the bigger and smaller tides.",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u06-l19.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U06-L19-ACTIVITY-015",
      "SourceSection": "19.2: Watching the Evening Sky",
      "SourceExcerpt": "\\(\\frac{2\\pi}{12}\\) makes the period 12 hours.",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u06-l19.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U06-L19-ACTIVITY-016",
      "SourceSection": "19.2: Watching the Evening Sky",
      "SourceExcerpt": "-1 translates the sine graph to the right by 1 hour to so it has a value of 0 at about 1 hour after midnight.",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u06-l19.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
